{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law","requirement":"Landlord may not demand a security deposit over 1.5 months' rent; annual increases are capped at 10%. The deposit must be held in trust, interest paid to the tenant, and returned with deductions within 30 days after tenancy.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent max deposit; 10% max annual increase; 30-day return","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey, except seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days. Applies to landlords receiving security deposits.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Seasonal rentals exempt; unit-count rules for deposit accounts (10 or more units)."},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days; excludes seasonal, temporary, or migrant farm worker housing from that exemption.","penalty":"Double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act due to domestic violence, the landlord must return the security deposit plus interest within 15 business days after termination and notify the tenant within 3 business days where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days return deadline; 3 business days notice","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence; does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Victims of domestic violence terminating lease; transient/seasonal rentals exempt."},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"If a tenant terminates the lease agreement prior to the expiration of  the lease pursuant to the Safe Housing Act , (N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6), the tenant is entitled to the return of their security deposit. Within 15 business days after the lease  is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
